\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N=\{1,2,\ldots\}$, and $\mathbb Z,\mathbb Q,\mathbb R,\mathbb C$ denote the integers, rationals, reals and complex numbers. Any other conventions are specified locally.


For an entire function $f$, write $f^{\circ0}(z)=z$ and $f^{\circ(n+1)}=f\circ f^{\circ n}$. Its Fatou set is the set on which the iterates form a normal family: every sequence has a subsequence converging locally uniformly in the spherical metric to a meromorphic function or to $\infty$. A Fatou component is a connected component of this set.
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Do there exist an entire function $f$, a Fatou component $\Omega$, and a single constant $R<\infty$ such that
\[|f^{\circ n}(z)|\leq R\quad(z\in\Omega,\ n\geq0),\qquad
f^{\circ n}(\Omega)\cap f^{\circ m}(\Omega)=\varnothing\quad(n\ne m)?\] \href{https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.07200}{[S2]}

\subsection{Short English statement}
Can a wandering Fatou component have all its forward images inside one fixed bounded disk?

